{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And I brought them into the land of their enemies.</b> When the exiles returned to the land of Israel by the decree of Cyrus king of Persia, the land was under the dominion of the nations, as it says (Nehemiah 9:36–37): וְהָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר נָתַתָּה לַאֲבֹתֵינוּ לֶאֱכֹל אֶת פִּרְיָהּ וְאֶת טוּבָהּ, הִנֵּה אֲנַחְנוּ עֲבָדִים עָלֶיהָ. וּתְבוּאָתָהּ מַרְבָּה לַמְּלָכִים אֲשֶׁר נָתַתָּה עָלֵינוּ בְּחַטֹּאתֵינוּ (\"The land that You gave to our fathers to eat its fruit and its goodness — behold, we are slaves upon it, and its produce is multiplied to the kings whom You have set over us for our sins\")."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:22.748337687Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}